          "worked": "At $x=-1$:\n\n$$\\begin{align*}-(-1)&=1\\\\\\frac{-1+3}{2}&=1\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe middle branch includes $(-1,1)$, so the left and middle branches join without a hole.\n\nAt $x=1$:\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{1+3}{2}&=2\\\\2(1)&=2\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe right branch includes $(1,2)$, so the middle and right branches also join without a hole. Draw the restricted straight branches as shown. The middle segment crosses the $y$-axis at $\\frac{3}{2}$.",
